hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17351","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, he said haddathana Sufyan, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umarah ibn Ruwaybah al-Thaqafi, he said: He saw Bishr ibn Marwan raising his hands on Friday, so he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the pulpit on Friday, and he said nothing except like this, and he pointed with his forefinger."
"17352","Haddathana Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Imarah ibn Ruwaybah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Sufyan once said: He heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: None who prayed before sunrise and before sunset will enter the Fire. It was said to Sufyan: From whom did you hear it. He said: From Umarah ibn Ruwaybah."
"17353","Haddathana Waki, from Sufyan, from Husayn, that Bishr ibn Marwan raised his hands on Friday upon the pulpit, so Umarah ibn Ruwaybah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did no more than this, and he pointed with his forefinger."
"17354","Haddathana Waki, from Sufyan, he said, and haddathana Abu al-Walid Hisham and Affan, they said haddathana Abu Awanah, from Abd al-Malik, Affan said haddathana Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ibn Imarah ibn Ruwaybah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: None who prayed before sunrise and before sunset will enter the Fire. And with him was a man, Affan said: from the people of Basrah, so he said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes, I testify to it against him. He said: And I testify, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying it in the place you heard it from him. Affan said: in it."
"17355","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa, he said haddathana Shayban, from Abd al-Malik, from Ibn Umarah ibn Ruwaybah al-Thaqafi, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None will enter the Fire, then he mentioned the like of it."
"17356","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Zuhayr, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: I was beside Imarah ibn Ruwaybah, and Bishr was addressing us, so when he supplicated he raised his hands, so Imarah said, meaning: May Allah disgrace these two hands, or these two little hands, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was addressing, when he supplicated he said like this, and he raised the forefinger alone."
"18486","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Abu Bakr ibn Umarah ibn Ruwaybah narrated to us, from his father who said: A man of the people of Basrah asked him, he said: Inform me of what you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None who prayed before the rising of the sun and before it sets will enter the Fire, he said: Did you hear it from him, he said: My ears heard it and my heart retained it, so the man said: By Allah, I heard him say that."
"18487","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: And Misar narrated to us, he said: And al-Bakhtari ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Abi Bakr ibn Umarah ibn Ruwaybah al-Thaqafi, they heard him from his father who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man who prayed before the rising of the sun and before its setting will enter the Fire, so a man of the people of Basrah said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Yes, he said: I testify that my ears heard it and my heart retained it."
"18488","Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ruwaybah that he saw Bishr ibn Marwan on the pulpit raising his hands pointing with his two fingers supplicating, so he said: Allah curse these two little hands, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the pulpit supplicating while pointing with one finger."
